<title>ZIMBABWE: RIO TINTO'S Q4 GOLD OUTPUT DOWN.</title>
<headline>RIO TINTO'S Q4 GOLD OUTPUT DOWN.</headline>
<dateline>HARARE 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>One of Zimbabwe's largest gold producers, Rio Tinto mined 18,226 ounces of gold in the fourth quarter of 1996 compared to 21,955 ounces in the previous December quarter.</p>
<p>In a statement, the company put total output for 1996 at 79,784 ounces versus 85,721 ounces previously.</p>
<p>The drop in production was in line with a cautionary statement Rio Tinto made last August when its Cam Dump reverted to a high throughput of generally low grade material.</p>
<p>-- Emelia Sithole, Harare Newsroom: +263-4 72 52 27/8/9</p>
</text>
